# Guessing game — an M0 validation program (00 §33.1).
#
# The computer picks a secret number; you guess until you find it. Too low or
# too high tells you which way to move. `random from 1 to 100` seeds the game;
# `number from` parses the guess and `attempt` keeps a typo from crashing it.

function read guess
    takes number called turn
    returns a number
    can fail
    make answer equal to ask "guess {turn}: "
    gives back attempt number from answer

make secret equal to random from 1 to 100
make changing guesses equal to 0
make changing found equal to false
make changing guess equal to 0

repeat while found is equal to false
    increase guesses by 1
    attempt read guess (guesses) if it fails then
        say "that was not a number — try again"
        decrease guesses by 1
    otherwise
        set guess to result
        if guess is equal to secret
            say "correct!"
            set found to true
        otherwise if guess is less than secret
            say "too low"
        otherwise
            say "too high"

say "you found it in {guesses} guesses!"
